<style>
  /* (X)RUNWAY lesson HUD REV2 - first-person trainee panel, faithful to the
     founder's hand sketch: header (NAME/ID | LESSON + TITLE box | TIME box),
     instruction box + quote, live metrics M1-M7 with checkboxes, summary,
     footer (LOCATION: AR + controls).

     Colors are BRAND_CSS twins (src/theme.ts):
       bg #0a0c10 . bgDeep #05070a . accent #4b9cd3 (Carolina Blue)
       accentSoft #8ec4e8 . accentDeep #2f7cb3 . white #f2f5f8 . silver #8a8f96
     Chrome neutrals derived from the cool bg family:
       glass #10151b . track #161c23 . border #232a33 . border-soft #1a2027
       check-off border #2f3a47 (mirrored in src/hud.ts CHECK_OFF_* consts).

     ASCII punctuation ONLY - the panel font has no middle-dot, em-dash or
     curly quote glyphs. Straight quotes and hyphens only. */

  /* Border tier system (premium pass 2026-07-10): edge light comes from
     BORDER COLOR contrast, not lighting. uikit's border-bend bevel was
     tried and REMOVED - the panel renders with the default unlit
     MeshBasicMaterial, whose shader never runs the bend (verified in
     @pmndrs/uikit shader.js), and switching to a lit panel-material-class
     let the scene's dim lights crush the brand colors (the START pill went
     near-black in the experiment). Tiers: light rims on primary surfaces
     (#8ec4e8 on accent pills, #f2f5f8 lip on the medal, #2c3540 on the
     title box), standard #232a33 on controls, #1d242e groove edges on the
     metric tracks/bars. Hairline dividers stay untinted. */
  .hud-root {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    width: 60;
    padding: 2.6;
    gap: 1.5;
    background-color: #0a0c10;
    border-color: #2a333f;
    border-width: 0.12;
    border-radius: 2.8;
  }

  /* ---------- header: MATT - ID 001 | LESSON 01 + BEGINNER WALK | TIME ---------- */

  .header-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding-bottom: 1.2;
    border-bottom-width: 0.07;
    border-color: #1a2027;
  }

  /* Stacked ident (name over ID) - the single-row "MATT - ID 001" overflowed
     its 14-wide box and wrapped mid-id in the headset (founder's photo). A
     column never overflows horizontally and frees width for the lesson title. */
  /* Header column widths + title metrics sized so both UI-reachable mode
     labels fit the middle slot on ONE line (premium pass 2026-07-10 - the
     founder's screenshot showed "BEGINNER WALK" wrapping): with the real
     Inter MSDF advances at 1.7/0.3, BEGINNER WALK = ~21.9 and EMERGING
     RUNWAY = ~25.6 + box padding 3.78 vs 54.56 - 12 - 10 = ~32.5
     available. CAVEAT: the founder-hidden legacy labels (COMMERCIAL
     MODELING ~30.9 borderline, PERFORMANCE CHALLENGE ~33.9 overflows) can
     resurface via a stale xrunway.mode.v1 localStorage pref and the
     21-cap one still wraps - retire those labels or clear the pref before
     ever re-surfacing the mode picker. */
  .ident {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.15;
    width: 12;
  }

  .ident-name {
    color: #f2f5f8;
    font-size: 1.7;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
  }

  .ident-id {
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
  }

  .lesson-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.55;
  }

  .lesson-no {
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.5;
  }

  .title-box {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center;
    padding-x: 1.8;
    padding-y: 0.75;
    background-color: #10151b;
    border-width: 0.09;
    border-color: #2c3540;
    border-radius: 1;
  }

  .title-text {
    color: #f2f5f8;
    font-size: 1.7;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
  }

  .time-wrap {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 0.5;
    width: 10;
  }

  .time-label {
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.5;
  }

  .time-box {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 9;
    padding-y: 0.65;
    background-color: #10151b;
    border-width: 0.09;
    border-color: #2f7cb3;
    border-radius: 1;
  }

  .time-val {
    color: #4b9cd3;
    font-size: 2.1;
    font-weight: bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
  }

  /* ---------- shared section / buttons ---------- */

  .section {
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.3;
  }

  .pill {
    padding-x: 1.5;
    padding-y: 1.1;
    border-radius: 2.2;
    font-size: 1.35;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.15;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* Primary pills carry a light accent rim (the web pass's lit convex CTA
     read); glass pills go a shade deeper so they read as outlines. */
  .pill-accent {
    background-color: #4b9cd3;
    color: #05070a;
    border-width: 0.09;
    border-color: #8ec4e8;
  }

  .pill-accent:hover {
    background-color: #2f7cb3;
    border-color: #8ec4e8;
  }

  .pill-glass {
    background-color: #0d1218;
    color: #f2f5f8;
    border-width: 0.09;
    border-color: #232a33;
  }

  .pill-glass:hover {
    border-color: #4b9cd3;
    color: #8ec4e8;
  }

  /* Quiet reference pills (Details / Scoring): links recede, actions stand
     forward - breaks the settings chip wall into tiers (premium pass). */
  .pill-ref {
    background-color: #0a0c10;
    color: #8a8f96;
    border-width: 0.08;
    border-color: #1a2027;
    padding-y: 0.85;
    font-size: 1.25;
  }

  .pill-ref:hover {
    border-color: #4b9cd3;
    color: #8ec4e8;
  }

  /* ---------- brief: instruction box + quote ---------- */

  .instruction-box {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.1;
    padding: 1.8;
    background-color: #10151b;
    border-width: 0.07;
    border-color: #1a2027;
    border-radius: 1.6;
  }

  .instruction {
    color: #f2f5f8;
    font-size: 1.9;
    line-height: 145%;
  }

  .quote-wrap {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border-left-width: 0.25;
    border-color: #4b9cd3;
    padding-left: 1.2;
  }

  .quote {
    color: #8ec4e8;
    font-size: 1.9;
    line-height: 145%;
  }

  /* Pass bar + target pace for the active mode (small, factual). */
  .brief-bar {
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.4;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* One-line coach-voice mention (#20/#48): mid-walk the trainee faces AWAY
     from this panel, so the brief says once that the coach will SPEAK. */
  .brief-coach {
    color: #5f666e;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.4;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* Wave 1 FIT guidance line: painted from globals.bodyFitFlow while a fit
     runs (showPhase stays idle, so the brief section is on screen). Hidden
     by hud.ts when no flow is live; the "..." placeholder is LOAD-BEARING
     (an empty text element compiles to a childless Container). */
  .bodyfit-line {
    color: #4b9cd3;
    font-size: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: 0.4;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* Wave 1 FIT settings-row status ("Fit: not set" / "Fit: set 3d ago"). */
  .bodyfit-status {
    color: #c7ccd2;
    font-size: 1.35;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  /* ---------- live: M1-M7 chip + label + bar + value + checkbox ---------- */

  #live-section {
    display: none;
  }

  #phase-line {
    color: #4b9cd3;
    font-size: 4.2;
    font-weight: bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.6;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 0.4;
    margin-bottom: 0.8;
  }

  .metric-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1;
  }

  .chip {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 3.4;
    padding-y: 0.35;
    background-color: #161c23;
    border-width: 0.06;
    border-color: #232a33;
    border-radius: 0.5;
  }

  .chip-text {
    color: #4b9cd3;
    font-size: 1.3;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.2;
  }

  .metric-label {
    width: 11;
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.22;
  }

  /* Inset groove edge - the accent fill runs inside a rimmed channel. */
  .metric-track {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-grow: 1;
    height: 1;
    background-color: #161c23;
    border-width: 0.06;
    border-color: #1d242e;
    border-radius: 0.5;
  }

  .metric-fill {
    width: 0%;
    height: 100%;
    background-color: #4b9cd3;
    border-radius: 0.5;
  }

  .metric-val {
    width: 4.2;
    color: #f2f5f8;
    font-size: 1.5;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .check {
    width: 1.7;
    height: 1.7;
    background-color: #10151b;
    border-width: 0.12;
    border-color: #2f3a47;
    border-radius: 0.4;
  }

  /* ---------- summary: as v1 + final checks ---------- */

  #summary-section {
    display: none;
  }

  /* Summary hierarchy (premium pass): four distinct steps under the score -
     6.0 bold white score, 1.8 semibold colored verdict, 1.4 accentSoft
     delta, 1.25 quiet stat. The founder's screenshot showed these stacked
     at near-equal weight. */
  .summary-header {
    color: #5f6a74;
    font-size: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: 0.9;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 0.6;
  }

  #overall-score {
    color: #f2f5f8;
    /* 6 (was 9): the summary section grew verdict/stat/coach-note rows past
       the panel's maxWidth/maxHeight aspect bound, which shrinks the WHOLE
       panel (every font) at the score reveal. A smaller hero number keeps the
       stack closer to width-bound; still ~3x the body copy. */
    font-size: 6;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* ---------- the medal badge (shares the hero row - no stack growth) ---------- */

  .hero-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5;
  }

  .medal {
    display: none;
    background-color: #d9b78a;
    border-width: 0.08;
    border-color: #f2f5f8;
    border-radius: 1.4;
    padding-x: 1.2;
    padding-y: 0.7;
  }

  .medal-text {
    color: #0a0c10;
    font-size: 1.4;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
  }

  /* PASS / NEEDS WORK vs the mode's own bar. hud.ts recolors per verdict. */
  #sum-verdict {
    color: #4b9cd3;
    font-size: 1.8;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.5;
    text-align: center;
  }

  #delta-line {
    color: #8ec4e8;
    font-size: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: 0.5;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* Ranking-medal caption (F.24): the medal is a personal RANK, the verdict is
     the absolute bar - so a gold can sit beside NEEDS WORK. hud.ts fills it
     from MEDAL_RANK_NOTE and reveals it only when a medal shows (display:none
     otherwise, the sum-carriage pattern). Quietest line in the stack - well
     under the settings-section height bound (one short caption). */
  #medal-note {
    display: none;
    color: #5f6a74;
    font-size: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: 0.2;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 0.2;
  }

  /* Duration + real steps/cadence, e.g. "58S ON THE RUNWAY - 58 STEPS - 96/MIN". */
  #sum-stat {
    color: #5f6a74;
    font-size: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: 0.5;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 0.8;
  }

  /* M8 head-carriage line, e.g. "HEAD CARRIAGE - CHIN LEVEL 84% - FACING ON
     LINE 91% - 1 HEAD DROP". Hidden until hud.ts fills it per summary (the
     coach-note pattern; stays hidden when the channel never engaged). */
  #sum-carriage {
    display: none;
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 0.8;
  }

  /* M10 hold line, e.g. "HOLD 1.6S - STILL 2.4 CM - MARK 12 CM" (or the
     NO READ branches). Hidden until hud.ts fills it from a director-built
     summary (the sum-carriage pattern). */
  #sum-hold {
    display: none;
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 0.8;
  }

  /* M9 beat line, e.g. "BEAT LOCK 78% - GRID 61/MIN - 34 STRIKES" (or the
     NO READ reason branches). Hidden until hud.ts fills it from a
     director-built summary (the sum-hold pattern; summary row order
     HOLD -> BEAT, adjudication G). */
  #sum-beat {
    display: none;
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 0.8;
  }

  /* M11 turn line, e.g. "TURN 1.2S - ONE MOTION - DIP 2 CM - LINE IN 0.8S"
     (or the NO READ reason branches). Hidden until hud.ts fills it from a
     summary whose analyzer ran (the both-null stamps hide it; summary row
     order HOLD -> BEAT -> TURN, adjudication G). */
  #sum-turn {
    display: none;
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 0.8;
  }

  /* M12 consistency line, e.g. "5 MATCHED WALKS: PACE SPREAD 3%, CADENCE 4%".
     Hidden until hud.ts fills it (the sum-carriage pattern; stays hidden
     until 3 matched walks exist for the current trainee). */
  #sum-repeat {
    display: none;
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 0.8;
  }

  /* F.27 head-motion observation notes (hold dwell + turn smoothness). A
     quiet, unlit gray read - color contrast carries it (border-tier law, no
     bevel), and the neutral gray keeps it clearly an OBSERVATION, not a scored
     coach note (accent-ruled) or a metric bar. Hidden until hud.ts fills it;
     one short line each, gated so at most two show (well under the
     settings-section height bound). */
  .obs-note {
    display: none;
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
    line-height: 130%;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 0.4;
  }

  /* Coach's notes - up to three short corrective lines under the scores.
     Hidden until hud.ts fills them per summary (unused slots stay hidden). */
  /* Accent-ruled like the web landing's coach/quote blocks - the same
     visual sentence on both surfaces (web parity pass 2026-07-10). */
  .coach-note {
    display: none;
    color: #c7ccd2;
    font-size: 1.3;
    line-height: 140%;
    border-left-width: 0.25;
    border-color: #4b9cd3;
    padding-left: 1.2;
  }

  /* The metric rows' card surface - the web summary's glass rows region.
     Tight padding: summary is not the height-binding state (settings is),
     but the hero score row above must keep its clearance. */
  .score-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background-color: #10151b;
    border-width: 0.07;
    border-color: #1a2027;
    border-radius: 1.6;
    padding-x: 1.4;
    padding-y: 0.5;
  }

  /* No hairline-under-every-row (the AI-tell the skill bans); the rows
     breathe on padding alone. */
  .score-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding-y: 0.55;
  }

  .score-label {
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: 0.22;
  }

  .score-right {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1;
  }

  .score-val {
    width: 4.2;
    color: #f2f5f8;
    font-size: 1.6;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .button-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    gap: 1.2;
    margin-top: 0.4;
  }

  .pill-grow {
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  /* ---------- mapping: walk-and-place runway onto the real floor ---------- */

  #map-section {
    display: none;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.4;
    align-items: center;
  }

  /* The mapping screens read as a guided moment (premium pass): kicker ->
     accent rule -> big prompt -> measured note -> paired pills. The empty
     space becomes intentional framing, keynote-title-slide rhythm. */
  .map-kicker {
    color: #5f6a74;
    font-size: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: 1;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 1.6;
  }

  .map-rule {
    width: 8;
    height: 0.16;
    border-radius: 0.5;
    background-color: #4b9cd3;
    align-self: center;
    margin-top: 0.9;
  }

  .map-prompt {
    color: #4b9cd3;
    font-size: 2.9;
    font-weight: bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.35;
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 130%;
    margin-top: 0.8;
    margin-bottom: 0.8;
  }

  .map-note {
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.4;
    line-height: 145%;
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 40;
    align-self: center;
  }

  .map-buttons {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    gap: 1.2;
    margin-top: 1.6;
  }

  /* ---------- fit-to-room status (#15): one line above the footer ----------
     Hidden until MappingSystem publishes a fit edge; hud.ts recolors per
     status (silver searching / red no-floor hint / accent fitted). */

  .fit-status {
    display: none;
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.3;
    line-height: 140%;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* ---------- tracking source (#32/#46): strip above the footer ----------
     Which body-tracking source is scoring (camera skeleton vs head-only).
     hud.ts drives #track-src text + color (accent = camera, silver = head). */

  .track-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  /* ---------- footer: LOCATION: AR + controls ---------- */

  .footer {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1;
    padding-top: 1.2;
    border-top-width: 0.07;
    border-color: #1a2027;
  }

  .location-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
  }

  .loc-caps {
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
  }

  .loc-caps-accent {
    color: #4b9cd3;
    font-size: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
  }

  .footer-buttons {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1;
  }

  /* ---------- settings: grouped runway + mode editor ---------- */

  #settings-section {
    display: none;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.7;
  }

  .set-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .set-title {
    color: #f2f5f8;
    font-size: 2;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.2;
  }

  .set-done {
    background-color: #10151b;
    color: #8ec4e8;
    border-width: 0.08;
    border-color: #232a33;
    border-radius: 2.4;
    padding-x: 1.5;
    padding-y: 0.8;
    font-size: 1.3;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
  }

  .set-done:hover {
    border-color: #4b9cd3;
  }

  /* Section labels earn legibility from weight + tracking + one contrast
     tier - NOT size (same font-size = zero cost on the height budget; the
     founder's screenshot flagged these as barely legible). */
  /* Kickers carry the web landing's accent-kicker language (the .kicker
     Carolina label over every web card) - instantly the same brand voice. */
  .set-kicker {
    color: #4b9cd3;
    font-size: 1.15;
    font-weight: medium;
    letter-spacing: 0.75;
    margin-top: 0.4;
  }

  /* The ADVANCED kicker recedes on purpose (founder call 2026-07-18):
     smallest type, dimmest neutral - the accent voice is NOT spent here. */
  .set-kicker-dim {
    color: #5f666e;
    font-size: 1.0;
    letter-spacing: 0.75;
    margin-top: 0.6;
  }

  .set-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    gap: 0.7;
  }

  /* ---------- details: the mode + music-tempo reference subsection ---------- */

  #details-section {
    display: none;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.7;
  }

  .det-name {
    color: #f2f5f8;
    font-size: 1.5;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.3;
    margin-top: 0.3;
  }

  .det-fact {
    color: #8ec4e8;
    font-size: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: 0.25;
  }

  .det-note {
    color: #c7ccd2;
    font-size: 1.2;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  /* ---------- scoring: the UNDERSTANDING THE SCORE education subsection ----------
     The XR twin of the landing #scoring-block; same text hierarchy as the web
     (.score-math silver, .scoring-sensor accent-soft), sized a notch under the
     det- tiers so the three wrapped formula lines keep the section inside the
     panel's aspect bound (no scrolling exists - a too-tall section shrinks
     the WHOLE panel). */

  #scoring-section {
    display: none;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.7;
  }

  /* The formula sits in its own boxed surface - the twin of the web
     education block's bordered score-math boxes (web parity pass). */
  .edu-math {
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.1;
    line-height: 1.35;
    background-color: #10151b;
    border-width: 0.06;
    border-color: #1a2027;
    border-radius: 0.8;
    padding-x: 1;
    padding-y: 0.7;
  }

  .edu-sensor {
    color: #8ec4e8;
    font-size: 1.1;
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin-top: 0.4;
  }

  /* F.17 provenance: the cited industry instruction under each formula. */
  .edu-src {
    color: #5f6a74;
    font-size: 1.05;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  /* Base values mirror hud.ts setChipActive's INACTIVE write - the two
     must move together (the runtime stamps these after first update). */
  .seg {
    flex-grow: 1;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 1.35;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    padding-y: 1.15;
    border-radius: 1.6;
    background-color: #0d1218;
    color: #c7ccd2;
    border-width: 0.08;
    border-color: #232a33;
  }

  .seg:hover {
    border-color: #4b9cd3;
    color: #8ec4e8;
  }

  .seg-sm {
    flex-grow: 1;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 1.2;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    padding-y: 1;
    border-radius: 1.4;
    background-color: #10151b;
    color: #c7ccd2;
    border-width: 0.08;
    border-color: #232a33;
  }

  .seg-sm:hover {
    border-color: #4b9cd3;
    color: #8ec4e8;
  }

  .adj {
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85;
    background-color: #10151b;
    border-width: 0.07;
    border-color: #1d2530;
    border-radius: 1.6;
    padding-x: 1.3;
    padding-y: 1.1;
  }

  .adj-top {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .adj-label {
    color: #c7ccd2;
    font-size: 1.35;
  }

  .adj-ctrl {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.1;
  }

  /* Fixed-size keycaps read as physical buttons. */
  .step {
    width: 3.7;
    height: 3.7;
    border-radius: 1.1;
    background-color: #161d26;
    color: #8ec4e8;
    border-width: 0.08;
    border-color: #2b3540;
    font-size: 2.1;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .step:hover {
    border-color: #4b9cd3;
  }

  .adj-val {
    color: #f2f5f8;
    font-size: 1.5;
    font-weight: semi-bold;
    width: 6.5;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .bar {
    height: 0.42;
    border-radius: 1;
    background-color: #222b35;
    border-width: 0.05;
    border-color: #1d242e;
  }

  /* 0.32 = the track's 0.42 minus its 2 x 0.05 border: yoga insets children
     by the border, so a full-height fill would overhang the groove's bottom
     edge (review catch 2026-07-10). */
  .bar-fill {
    height: 0.32;
    border-radius: 1;
    background-color: #4b9cd3;
  }

  .set-foot {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    border-top-width: 0.07;
    border-color: #1a2027;
    padding-top: 1;
    margin-top: 0.3;
  }

  .set-foot-label {
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.3;
  }

  .set-foot-btns {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    gap: 0.8;
  }

  .mini {
    background-color: #10151b;
    color: #8ec4e8;
    border-width: 0.08;
    border-color: #232a33;
    border-radius: 1.2;
    padding-x: 1.3;
    padding-y: 0.85;
    font-size: 1.25;
  }

  .mini:hover {
    border-color: #4b9cd3;
  }

  .set-controls {
    color: #5f6a74;
    font-size: 1.05;
    line-height: 1.45;
    border-top-width: 0.07;
    border-color: #1a2027;
    padding-top: 0.85;
    margin-top: 0.5;
  }

  /* ---------- tutorial: the first-run in-headset guide (2026-07-11) ----------
     One card at a time (kicker + hero title + body + optional cadence track +
     dots/nav), so this section is well UNDER the tallest state (settings) - it
     never becomes the binding aspect-bound. Reuses the glass tiers, the
     Carolina .set-kicker voice, the .set-done header button, and the .pill
     family for nav; only the hero title, body, dots and the cadence track are
     new. Unlit-material law: edges are BORDER-COLOR tiers, never bevels. */

  #tutorial-section {
    display: none;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.1;
  }

  /* Hero cue - bigger + bolder than a section title (this IS the lesson). */
  .tut-title {
    color: #f2f5f8;
    font-size: 2.3;
    font-weight: bold;
    letter-spacing: 0.2;
    line-height: 118%;
  }

  .tut-body {
    color: #c7ccd2;
    font-size: 1.45;
    line-height: 145%;
  }

  /* Progress dots (one per card): the active dot fills Carolina + pops scale,
     stamped by hud.ts renderTutorialStep (paint-only, no relayout). */
  .tut-dots {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6;
  }

  .tut-dot {
    width: 1.1;
    height: 1.1;
    border-radius: 2;
    background-color: #2b3540;
  }

  /* The cadence track (PACE card only, #tutorial-section step 4): step pips
     light left-to-right to a slow beat so the trainee FEELS the rhythm before
     they walk it. hud.ts advances the lit pip; only ticks while this card is
     the visible tutorial card (frame-budget guard). Groove is the size-bar
     material (unlit, border-tier edge). */
  .tut-cad {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    background-color: #10151b;
    border-width: 0.06;
    border-color: #1a2027;
    border-radius: 0.9;
    padding-x: 1.3;
    padding-y: 1;
  }

  /* Preference pills (MAKE IT YOURS card only, #tutorial-section step 1):
     stacked set-rows of the same pill material as settings. */
  .tut-prefs {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.7;
  }

  .tut-pip {
    width: 1.5;
    height: 1.5;
    border-radius: 2;
    background-color: #222b35;
  }

  /* Live head-level indicator (CARRIAGE card only, #tutorial-section step 2):
     the learn-by-doing beat. hud.ts reads the LIVE head pitch off player.head
     each frame and slides the marker so the trainee proves the headset sees
     their head BEFORE any score is at stake. Marker + zone glow Carolina when
     the head is level; the label reads the correction otherwise. Shown/hidden
     per step (the tut-cad precedent), paint-only, unlit border-tier material. */
  .tut-level {
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.7;
  }

  .tut-level-track {
    width: 34;
    height: 2.4;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background-color: #10151b;
    border-width: 0.06;
    border-color: #1a2027;
    border-radius: 1.2;
  }

  /* The centered LEVEL zone - where the head reads level (the +-7 deg carriage
     band). Its border glows Carolina when the marker is inside it. */
  .tut-level-zone {
    width: 10;
    height: 1.5;
    border-radius: 0.9;
    border-width: 0.08;
    border-color: #2b3540;
    background-color: #141b22;
  }

  /* The moving marker - absolutely centered over the zone (position maps to
     yoga positionType), hud.ts translateX-es it with the live head pitch.
     Carolina when level, dim otherwise. */
  .tut-level-marker {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1.6;
    height: 2;
    border-radius: 0.7;
    background-color: #2b3540;
  }

  .tut-level-label {
    color: #8a8f96;
    font-size: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: 0.25;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* Bottom nav: dots on the left, Back/Next on the right. */
  .tut-nav {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.9;
    margin-top: 0.3;
  }

  .tut-nav-btns {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    gap: 0.8;
  }
</style>
<div id="hud-root" class="hud-root">
  <div class="header-row">
    <div class="ident">
      <span id="ident-name" class="ident-name">TRAINEE</span>
      <span id="ident-id" class="ident-id"> - ID 001</span>
    </div>
    <div class="lesson-block">
      <span id="lesson-no" class="lesson-no">LESSON 01</span>
      <div class="title-box">
        <span id="title-text" class="title-text">BEGINNER WALK</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="time-wrap">
      <span class="time-label">TIME</span>
      <div class="time-box">
        <span id="time-box" class="time-val">60S</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="brief-section" class="section">
    <div id="instruction-box" class="instruction-box">
      <span id="instruction" class="instruction">Stand tall, eyes on one far point. Long strides - one foot in front of the other, down the invisible line. Steady to the beat. Hit the mark, hold, then bring it home.</span>
      <div class="quote-wrap">
        <span class="quote">"I don't see the audience. I hear the music." - Naomi Campbell</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <span id="brief-bar" class="brief-bar">PASS AT 78 - TARGET 0.85 M/S</span>
    <span id="bodyfit-line" class="bodyfit-line">...</span>
    <!-- Controls legend (tester catch 2026-07-09): the main-surface twin of
         the settings set-controls line - trigger / slide / snap turn /
         teleport were disclosed nowhere on this surface. Static mechanical
         control tokens (COPY-WORKSHEET law: mechanical labels are exempt
         from the founder-words law). Lives INSIDE the brief so it shows
         only in idle/brief - the phases where these sticks are LIVE
         (hud-state.ts pauses slide/teleport/snap-turn mid-walk). -->
    <span class="set-controls">Controls - Trigger: click a button | Left stick: move | Right stick: snap turn | Right stick down: teleport | Left X/Y: fit to room | Right B: hide/show panel</span>
  </div>

  <div id="live-section" class="section">
    <span id="phase-line">STAND BY</span>
    <!-- Headset-only honest card: the head-measured metrics only. Element IDs
         (m2/m3/m4) are unchanged so hud.ts still maps them to pace/rhythm/
         footPlacement; POSTURE (m1) + the composites (m5/m6/m7) are cut. -->
    <div class="metric-row">
      <div class="chip"><span class="chip-text">M1</span></div>
      <span class="metric-label">PACE</span>
      <div class="metric-track">
        <div id="m2-fill" class="metric-fill"></div>
      </div>
      <span id="m2-val" class="metric-val">0</span>
      <div id="m2-check" class="check"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-row">
      <div class="chip"><span class="chip-text">M2</span></div>
      <span class="metric-label">CARRIAGE</span>
      <div class="metric-track">
        <div id="m3-fill" class="metric-fill"></div>
      </div>
      <span id="m3-val" class="metric-val">0</span>
      <div id="m3-check" class="check"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="metric-row">
      <div class="chip"><span class="chip-text">M3</span></div>
      <span class="metric-label">LINE</span>
      <div class="metric-track">
        <div id="m4-fill" class="metric-fill"></div>
      </div>
      <span id="m4-val" class="metric-val">0</span>
      <div id="m4-check" class="check"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="summary-section" class="section">
    <span class="summary-header">SCORED SUMMARY</span>
    <!-- MEDAL (founder call 2026-07-09): the badge shares the hero row with
         the number - ZERO stack growth against the aspect bound (the 9->6
         hero-font lesson above). Hidden until hud.ts pops it at the graded
         sting's +0.9 s anchor; the "-" placeholder is LOAD-BEARING. -->
    <div class="hero-row">
      <span id="overall-score">0</span>
      <div id="medal-badge" class="medal">
        <span id="medal-text" class="medal-text">-</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <span id="sum-verdict">PASS - BAR 78</span>
    <!-- Ranking-medal caption (F.24): tells the trainee the medal is a rank
         among their OWN walks (best = gold), NOT the pass bar - so a gold can
         sit beside NEEDS WORK. hud.ts writes MEDAL_RANK_NOTE + reveals it only
         when a medal shows. The "-" placeholder is LOAD-BEARING (an empty text
         element compiles to a childless Container hud.ts can't write into). -->
    <span id="medal-note">-</span>
    <span id="delta-line">FIRST WALK</span>
    <span id="sum-stat">0S ON THE RUNWAY</span>
    <span id="sum-carriage">HEAD CARRIAGE</span>
    <!-- Honest shipped card: PACE / CARRIAGE / LINE (the head-measured reads) +
         the HEAD CARRIAGE row above. POSTURE + the composites (presence/
         confidence/presentation) and the HOLD/BEAT/TURN/CONSISTENCY riders
         are cut. Element IDs (s2/s3/s4) are unchanged so hud.ts keeps mapping
         them to pace/rhythm/footPlacement. -->
    <!-- The metric rows sit on their own card surface (web parity pass:
         the landing's glass sum-rows region). No ids on the wrapper. -->
    <div id="score-card" class="score-card">
      <div class="score-row">
        <span class="score-label">M1 PACE</span>
        <div class="score-right">
          <span id="s2-val" class="score-val">0</span>
          <div id="s2-check" class="check"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="score-row">
        <span class="score-label">M2 CARRIAGE</span>
        <div class="score-right">
          <span id="s3-val" class="score-val">0</span>
          <div id="s3-check" class="check"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="score-row">
        <span class="score-label">M3 LINE</span>
        <div class="score-right">
          <span id="s4-val" class="score-val">0</span>
          <div id="s4-check" class="check"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- F.27 head-motion observation notes (hold DWELL + turn SMOOTHNESS):
         display-only reads answering "did I hold long enough / was my turn
         smooth", NOT scored metrics. Hidden until hud.ts fills them from a
         director summary that measured a hold/turn (a null read hides the
         line); the "-" placeholder is LOAD-BEARING (see the coach-note note
         below). Gray, unlit - distinct from the accent coach notes. -->
    <span id="sum-hold-note" class="obs-note">-</span>
    <span id="sum-turn-note" class="obs-note">-</span>
    <!-- The placeholder "-" is LOAD-BEARING: an EMPTY text element compiles to
         a childless Container (no Text child), and hud.ts setProperties({text})
         then has nothing to write into - the coach notes would never render.
         Hidden until hud.ts fills them (display:none via .coach-note). -->
    <span id="sum-note-1" class="coach-note">-</span>
    <span id="sum-note-2" class="coach-note">-</span>
    <span id="sum-note-3" class="coach-note">-</span>
    <div class="button-row">
      <button id="again-button" class="pill pill-accent pill-grow">WALK AGAIN</button>
      <!-- Replay Theater: plays the ghost of this walk on the runway - the
           trainee watches from where they stand (the rig is never moved in
           XR). hud.ts hides it when the walk is not replayable. -->
      <button id="replay-button" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">REPLAY</button>
    </div>
    <div class="button-row">
      <!-- THE WALK CARD's honest pill: the headset browser cannot save/share
           a composed image, so tapping this says where the card lives (label
           swap to SHARE_CARD_NOTE for a few seconds - hud.ts). -->
      <button id="share-button" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">SHARE CARD</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="map-section" class="section">
    <span class="map-kicker">MAP YOUR RUNWAY</span>
    <!-- Text-free accent rule (premium pass) - no id, invisible to hud.ts. -->
    <div class="map-rule"></div>
    <span id="map-prompt" class="map-prompt">STAND AT YOUR START - PRESS TRIGGER</span>
    <span id="map-note" class="map-note">Point at the floor with your right controller - the trigger drops your start point. CANCEL exits.</span>
    <div class="map-buttons">
      <button id="map-confirm" class="pill pill-accent pill-grow">CONFIRM</button>
      <button id="map-cancel" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">CANCEL</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- TUTORIAL (first-run in-headset guide, 2026-07-11). Auto-opens on the
       first XR entry (HUDSystem.onVisibility, gated on the xrunway.xr-tutorial.v1
       key + 0 walks), re-openable from Settings -> Guide. Placed BEFORE
       #settings-section deliberately: it sits outside every copy-slice test
       window (scoring/details/controls-legend all start at or after settings).
       All visible strings are written at runtime from TUTORIAL_STEPS
       (hud-copy.ts) into these fixed elements - the MAP_PROMPTS pattern - so
       the markup stays static + ASCII and the copy is drift-pinned by test.
       Placeholder text is LOAD-BEARING (an empty text element compiles to a
       childless Container that never renders). -->
  <div id="tutorial-section" class="section">
    <div class="set-head">
      <span id="tut-kicker" class="set-kicker">WELCOME</span>
      <button id="tut-skip" class="set-done">Skip</button>
    </div>
    <span id="tut-title" class="tut-title">You are the model.</span>
    <span id="tut-body" class="tut-body">Loading your first lesson...</span>
    <!-- Preference pills: MAKE IT YOURS card only (shown/hidden per step,
         founder call 2026-07-16 - novices set their toggles before any walk).
         Each writes the SAME shared signal its settings twin writes; labels
         are stamped at runtime by the same hud.ts update fns. Half-width
         pairs hold to the width-cap law (longest half label 15 chars); the
         beat pill is full-width ("Beat pulse: countdown" is the cap label
         and must not share a row - the b8c0ddf overlap lesson). -->
    <div id="tut-prefs" class="tut-prefs">
      <div class="set-row">
        <button id="tut-music" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Music: on</button>
        <button id="tut-mode" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Level: Beginner</button>
      </div>
      <div class="set-row">
        <button id="tut-bpm" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Music BPM: 100</button>
        <button id="tut-duration" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Duration: 20s</button>
      </div>
      <div class="set-row">
        <button id="tut-beat" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Beat pulse: countdown</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <!-- The cadence track: five step pips + hud.ts lights them in sequence on
         the PACE card only (shown/hidden per step). -->
    <div id="tut-cad" class="tut-cad">
      <div id="tut-pip-0" class="tut-pip"></div>
      <div id="tut-pip-1" class="tut-pip"></div>
      <div id="tut-pip-2" class="tut-pip"></div>
      <div id="tut-pip-3" class="tut-pip"></div>
      <div id="tut-pip-4" class="tut-pip"></div>
    </div>
    <!-- The live head-level indicator: CARRIAGE card only (shown/hidden per
         step). hud.ts reads the LIVE head pitch each frame and slides the
         marker so the trainee proves the headset sees their head before any
         score. Label text is written at runtime from TUT_LEVEL_LABELS
         (hud-copy.ts); the placeholder is LOAD-BEARING (non-empty). -->
    <div id="tut-level" class="tut-level">
      <div class="tut-level-track">
        <div id="tut-level-zone" class="tut-level-zone"></div>
        <div id="tut-level-marker" class="tut-level-marker"></div>
      </div>
      <span id="tut-level-label" class="tut-level-label">MOVE YOUR HEAD</span>
    </div>
    <div class="tut-nav">
      <div id="tut-dots" class="tut-dots">
        <div id="tut-dot-0" class="tut-dot"></div>
        <div id="tut-dot-1" class="tut-dot"></div>
        <div id="tut-dot-2" class="tut-dot"></div>
        <div id="tut-dot-3" class="tut-dot"></div>
        <div id="tut-dot-4" class="tut-dot"></div>
        <div id="tut-dot-5" class="tut-dot"></div>
        <div id="tut-dot-6" class="tut-dot"></div>
        <div id="tut-dot-7" class="tut-dot"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tut-nav-btns">
        <button id="tut-back" class="pill pill-glass">Back</button>
        <button id="tut-next" class="pill pill-accent">Next</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="settings-section" class="section">
    <div class="set-head">
      <span class="set-title">Your runway</span>
      <button id="set-done" class="set-done">Done</button>
    </div>

    <span class="set-kicker">SHAPE</span>
    <div class="set-row">
      <button id="set-shape-straight" class="seg">Straight</button>
      <button id="set-shape-t" class="seg">T</button>
      <button id="set-shape-x" class="seg">X</button>
      <button id="set-shape-u" class="seg">U</button>
    </div>

    <span class="set-kicker">SIZE</span>
    <div id="row-length" class="adj">
      <div class="adj-top">
        <span class="adj-label">Length</span>
        <div class="adj-ctrl">
          <button id="set-length-dec" class="step">-</button>
          <span id="set-length-val" class="adj-val">10.0 m</span>
          <button id="set-length-inc" class="step">+</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar"><div id="set-length-fill" class="bar-fill"></div></div>
    </div>
    <div id="row-width" class="adj">
      <div class="adj-top">
        <span class="adj-label">Width</span>
        <div class="adj-ctrl">
          <button id="set-width-dec" class="step">-</button>
          <span id="set-width-val" class="adj-val">1.4 m</span>
          <button id="set-width-inc" class="step">+</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar"><div id="set-width-fill" class="bar-fill"></div></div>
    </div>
    <div id="row-arm" class="adj">
      <div class="adj-top">
        <span class="adj-label">Arm span</span>
        <div class="adj-ctrl">
          <button id="set-arm-dec" class="step">-</button>
          <span id="set-arm-val" class="adj-val">3.0 m</span>
          <button id="set-arm-inc" class="step">+</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar"><div id="set-arm-fill" class="bar-fill"></div></div>
    </div>
    <div id="row-cross" class="adj">
      <div class="adj-top">
        <span class="adj-label">Cross point</span>
        <div class="adj-ctrl">
          <button id="set-cross-dec" class="step">-</button>
          <span id="set-cross-val" class="adj-val">50%</span>
          <button id="set-cross-inc" class="step">+</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bar"><div id="set-cross-fill" class="bar-fill"></div></div>
    </div>

    <span class="set-kicker">BODY FIT</span>
    <div class="set-row">
      <span id="set-bodyfit-status" class="bodyfit-status">Fit: not set</span>
      <button id="set-bodyfit-run" class="seg">Run fit</button>
    </div>

    <span class="set-kicker">ROOM</span>
    <div class="set-row">
      <button id="set-fit" class="pill pill-accent pill-grow">Fit to my room</button>
      <button id="set-crowd" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Crowd: on</button>
    </div>
    <!-- Coach voice pill REMOVED (founder ruling 2026-07-16, repeated from an
         earlier chat: the coach is text-only for this product - no spoken
         coaching, no toggle to suggest otherwise). -->
    <div class="set-row">
      <button id="set-music" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Music: on</button>
    </div>
    <div class="set-row">
      <button id="set-beat" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Beat pulse: countdown</button>
    </div>
    <!-- Floor-glow toggle (founder call 2026-07-13): the always-on blue warp
         rings on the live floor can distract (tester note); this gates them
         (the per-step ripples stay). Own row - "Beat pulse: countdown" is the
         width-cap label and must not share a row (the b8c0ddf overlap lesson). -->
    <!-- LEVEL (founder ruling 2026-07-15: make EMERGING reachable in-headset -
         the exec-review coach P0). A toggle pill, not the retired 4-chip mode
         row: only the two founder-named tiers are offered (the legacy
         COMMERCIAL/PERFORMANCE labels overflow the header title box - the
         in-file width caveat), and pairing it on the floor-glow row adds ZERO
         height to settings, the panel's aspect-bound tallest state. Both
         labels are mid-short (the Music BPM + Duration pairing precedent). -->
    <div class="set-row">
      <button id="set-level" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Level: Beginner</button>
      <button id="set-floorfx" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Floor glow: on</button>
    </div>
    <!-- Music tempo + walk duration pair (founder call 2026-07-09: 10-60 s,
         default 20 - hud.ts cycles the pref, ShowDirector locks it per run);
         the two short reference pills (Details + Scoring) pair on the next
         row. "Beat pulse: countdown" is the longest settings label and
         half-width would risk the exact overlap class the founder
         photographed (the b8c0ddf lesson) - "Music BPM: 100" and
         "Duration: 20s" are both mid-short; eyeball face-on + on-device. -->
    <div class="set-row">
      <button id="set-bpm" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Music BPM: 100</button>
      <button id="set-duration" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Duration: 20s</button>
    </div>
    <!-- Pace style (founder ask 2026-07-18): which side of the target speed
         the scoring forgives - "Confident stride" (default, fast is gentle)
         or "Take your time" (directors' orders - slow is gentle). Own row:
         "Pace style: Confident stride" is a width-cap-class label. -->
    <div class="set-row">
      <button id="set-pace-style" class="pill pill-glass pill-grow">Pace style: Confident stride</button>
    </div>
    <div class="set-row">
      <button id="set-details" class="pill pill-ref pill-grow">Details</button>
      <button id="set-scoring" class="pill pill-ref pill-grow">Scoring</button>
      <button id="set-guide" class="pill pill-ref pill-grow">Guide</button>
    </div>
    <!-- ADVANCED (deliberately the quietest thing in settings - founder call:
         hardest to find by design language: last row, dimmest kicker, a
         single ref-tier pill). Cycles the pace control-band half-width. -->
    <span class="set-kicker-dim">ADVANCED</span>
    <div class="set-row">
      <button id="set-pace-band" class="pill pill-ref pill-grow">Pace band: 0.10 m/s</button>
    </div>

    <!-- LESSON mode selector removed (founder call): modes aren't visibly
         differentiated yet, so the walk stays on the default. hud.ts's
         set-mode-0..3 onClick + modeChips lookups are ?.-guarded, so the
         missing elements are safe no-ops. Restore by re-adding this row. -->

    <div class="set-foot">
      <span class="set-foot-label">Preset</span>
      <div class="set-foot-btns">
        <button id="set-preset-prev" class="mini">Prev</button>
        <button id="set-preset-next" class="mini">Next</button>
        <button id="set-reset" class="mini">Reset</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <span class="set-controls">Controls - Left X/Y: fit to room | Right B: hide/show panel | Right stick: scrub a focused size</span>
  </div>

  <!-- SCORING (queue #5): the in-headset twin of the landing UNDERSTANDING
       THE SCORE block (index.html #scoring-block). Opened from settings via
       #set-scoring, #scoring-done returns (hud.ts applySections). The intro +
       the three metric definitions are the founder's own words (no-AI-text
       law) transliterated ONLY as the ASCII panel font demands (x for the
       times sign, deg for the degree sign, - for the em-dash, "and" for the
       ampersand); the "score =" lines are the ACTUAL scoring formulas
       (metrics.ts headset path / pose-derive.ts twin) - both surfaces are
       drift-pinned by test/scoring-copy.test.ts. -->
  <div id="scoring-section" class="section">
    <div class="set-head">
      <span class="set-title">Understanding the score</span>
      <button id="scoring-done" class="set-done">Done</button>
    </div>
    <span class="det-note">Here are how the 3 main metrics are defined, tracked, and what it means for you. Please note that the data for these metrics is tracked by the headset only.</span>
    <span class="det-name">PACE</span>
    <span class="det-note">head speed vs the target head speed</span>
    <span class="edu-math">score = 100 within 0.10 m/s of the target; slower costs 90 per m/s, faster costs 45 (40-100). In the band = 100.</span>
    <span class="edu-src">In the industry's words: "take long strides, and control your pace" - Naomi Campbell</span>
    <span class="det-name">CARRIAGE</span>
    <span class="det-note">% of time the head stays level (downward glances negatively affect this score)</span>
    <span class="edu-math">score = 40 + 60 x the share of the walk your head stayed level (chin within 7 deg of neutral) and facing down the line. A head-drop (>15 deg down) counts against it.</span>
    <span class="edu-src">In the industry's words: "keep your head straight and steady" - CM Models</span>
    <span class="det-name">LINE</span>
    <span class="det-note">head alignment with the center line</span>
    <span class="edu-math">score = 100 - (your average distance off the centerline, in meters) x 240 (40-100). Dead on the line = 100.</span>
    <span class="edu-src">In the industry's words: "walking along a thin, invisible line" - Backstage</span>
    <span class="edu-sensor">Computed on-device from Meta Quest 3 head tracking only - no camera, no body scan; nothing is scored that the headset did not measure.</span>
  </div>

  <!-- DETAILS (founder call 2026-07-08): the reference subsection for the
       mode differences + the music tempo options. Opened from settings via
       #set-details, #det-done returns to settings (hud.ts applySections).
       Every visible line is a structural label, the modes' own shipped
       chip facts (coach.ts targetPaceLabel/passBarLabel + the default
       tempo), or the founder's VERBATIM note (the no-AI-text law) -
       drift-pinned against the live constants by test/details-copy.test.ts.
       Only the two founder-named modes are listed (commercial/challenge
       tempo defaults are provisional - an open founder call). -->
  <div id="details-section" class="section">
    <div class="set-head">
      <span class="set-title">Details</span>
      <button id="det-done" class="set-done">Done</button>
    </div>

    <span class="set-kicker">MODES</span>
    <span class="det-name">BEGINNER WALK</span>
    <span class="det-fact">TARGET 0.85 M/S - PASS AT 78 - MUSIC 100 BPM</span>
    <span class="det-note">everyday walking speed or leisure</span>
    <span class="det-name">EMERGING RUNWAY</span>
    <span class="det-fact">TARGET 0.72 M/S - PASS AT 80 - MUSIC 125 BPM</span>
    <span class="det-note">emerging level walking speed (industry standard)</span>

    <span class="set-kicker">MUSIC BPM</span>
    <span class="det-note">62 - half time of the emerging level speed</span>
    <span class="det-note">100 - everyday walking speed or leisure</span>
    <span class="det-note">125 - emerging level walking speed (industry standard)</span>
  </div>

  <!-- Fit-to-room status (#15). The placeholder text is LOAD-BEARING: an empty
       text element compiles to a childless Container (no Text child) and could
       never render. Hidden until hud.ts shows it on a fit edge. -->
  <span id="fit-status" class="fit-status">Looking for your floor...</span>

  <!-- Tracking source (#32/#46). "HEAD ONLY" placeholder is load-bearing (an
       empty text element can never render) AND the honest default. -->
  <div class="track-row">
    <span class="loc-caps">TRACKING: </span>
    <span id="track-src" class="loc-caps">HEAD ONLY</span>
  </div>

  <!-- LOCATION: AR label removed - the backdrop picker is gone (scene is always
       AR), so it was redundant AND it crowded the BEGIN WALK button (founder's
       photo). The 5 buttons now get the full footer width, centered. -->
  <div class="footer">
    <div class="footer-buttons">
      <!-- Founder B8.4/C8.3 (2026-07-09): "Start" - uikit has no
           text-transform, so the styled ALL-CAPS form is literal (the
           worksheet's caps law; the footer neighbors are all caps). -->
      <button id="begin-button" class="pill pill-accent">START</button>
      <button id="settings-button" class="pill pill-glass">SETTINGS</button>
      <button id="map-button" class="pill pill-glass">MAP</button>
      <button id="guide-button" class="pill pill-glass">GUIDE</button>
      <button id="reset-button" class="pill pill-glass">RESET</button>
      <button id="xr-button" class="pill pill-glass">EXIT</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
